<h2>Frequently asked interface questions</h2>
<h3>Does ICOM make any vehicle programming procedure safe?</h3><p>No. ICOM is only one part of an authorized workshop hardware and software environment. Vehicle power, approved programming software, supported interface firmware and technician procedure remain separate requirements.</p>
<h3>Is a K+DCAN cable automatically wrong on all F-series vehicles?</h3><p>No universal statement is safe. Certain vendor hardware/software combinations cover selected F-series tasks, but the exact vehicle, program and interface revision determine whether that applies. Do not substitute this generalized map for a verified application compatibility list.</p>
<h3>Can the same Bluetooth adapter be used with every diagnostic app?</h3><p>No. An app can require an exact adapter model, Bluetooth implementation or firmware even when the vehicle accepts the physical connection. Verify support separately for BimmerCode, BimmerLink, ProTool or other software.</p>